/*
 * ESP32-S3-N16R8 + 3.5" ILI9488 (480x320) SPI TFT
 * Web-controlled Clock + Weather station  (with WiFi setup hotspot)
 *
 * WIRING
 *   3V3->VCC  GND->GND  GPIO10->CS  GPIO12->RESET  GPIO11->DC/RS
 *   GPIO13->SDI(MOSI)  GPIO14->SCK  GPIO9->SDO(MISO)  GPIO8->LED(backlight)
 *
 * ARDUINO IDE SETTINGS
 *   Board: "ESP32S3 Dev Module"   (esp32 core 3.x)
 *   PSRAM: "OPI PSRAM"            Flash Size: 16MB   USB CDC On Boot: Enabled
 *   Libraries: LovyanGFX (by lovyan03), ArduinoJson 7.x
 *
 * WIFI SETUP (change WiFi any time)
 *   Start the hotspot by ANY of these:
 *     1. Web panel -> System -> "Hotspot" button
 *     2. Hold the BOOT button (GPIO0) for 2 seconds
 *     3. Automatic: WiFi not found at boot, or lost for 60 seconds
 *   Then: join WiFi "ESP32-Clock" (pass 12345678) -> page opens (or 192.168.4.1/wifi)
 *         -> pick your network from the list -> enter password -> Connect.
 *   The new network is tested first; if it fails the old one is restored.
 */

